 (notes
  "COMBINED NEITHER PASSES; no candidate; both flags stay default-off. C vs S NO-BUILD by the harm bar: L 63.9 % (3,646/5,707), F 90.6 % over 213 pairs; median delta ln -0.819 (delta 0.20, m_S 0.149), 0/5 positive (-0.810/-0.599/-0.819/-0.833/-0.931); D > 0 in 4/5, trim-3 > 0 in 0/5, arm-median maxDD +18.67 pp (S 24.6-32.1 -> C 41.4-45.5 %); CAGR -2.5..-3.9 pp/yr. G vs S INCONCLUSIVE (the D bar): G check 0; L 19.1 % (= the screen's 20 % base), F 90.6 % over 406; median -0.038 (-0.038/-0.067/+0.093/-0.123/+0.046), maxDD -0.27 pp; D > 0 in 2/5 (-3.24/-2.57/+0.75/-7.38/+2.43), trim-3 3/5. C vs G median -0.772, 0/5 -> admissions cost. CLASS: C REJECT-as-default / keep-as-axis (one window, N = 4 only; not bundled into a preset without a new mechanism argument); G no cells without a fresh rationale. Resolves the stale-e-cap-screen escalation (2026-11-12, Inconclusive). WHY C: the 15 % gate read at the capped E' admits 651-670 names/seed (~25/yr; stops 12.3-14.7 % below E', p10-p90) that S's gate rejects; the gate is the book's bear brake: S's lists in 2001/2002/2008 show 15-19 gate skips per placed ticket and S entered nothing in 2008 while the macro gate was open (Neutral) in the spring rally; C entered 20-23 names in 2008, 0 won (-17.5..-21.4 NAV-%/seed), lost 2000-02 too, and its max DD is one episode, 2007-07-19 -> 2009-07-08, in every seed (S over the same dates -7.5..-19.2 %). Elsewhere the admissions fill the book (C 70 % invested, 7.5 positions vs S 56 %, 5.3; C 95-96 % invested on the Fridays it placed nothing) and crowd out S's better names: 267-294 S tickets/seed, -167..-207 NAV-%; ADSK 2003, APPS 2020, MMYT 2023 alone -101.5/seed. Admissions on their own +64..+88/seed (bear years -38.6..-53.3, recoveries 2003+2009 +37.3..+49.4, DEG 2014 +26.9) but median -5 %/trade, p25 a full stop, top-3 removed +6..+28. D (re-pricing) -1.6..+3.9. WHY G: same-week capped fills +4.15..+5.82 NAV-%/seed (price + size, exit 0); earlier fills -0.90..-4.96: laggard rotation (hysteresis 2, 13-week RS) ejects early fills inside the unbroken base. ROL 2016-09-02: G filled week 0, rotated after 26 d at -0.6 %; S filled 7 weeks later on the breakout, +52.5 % = -4.79/seed (ex-ROL D > 0 in 4/5); LMT 2017 -1.05/seed; cash at the fill WING 2017, ENB 2004. The screen held exits fixed: 60-72 % of its H2' gain came from earlier fills credited with the null's exit. DEFECTS: k1/k4 pack renders half blank and silent (re-render; add a blank-slice check); V7/V13 include chain-w D1 artifacts (C's V7 222-223 vs 32-36 mostly Virgin_territory enrichment); a stop traded days before the exit fill: TRW-wein-742 (C, 2008, all seeds), RGP 2013 (C), CAL-wein-719 (G), none in S, #3075 class. FORWARD: stop the stale-E line; the stale E is load-bearing; any lever that moves the gate's effective distance is read for positions count, by-year admissions and crowded-out S tickets; entry-timing screens must replay exits from the moved fill. Writeup: dev/experiments/stale-e-cap-k5-2026-11-14/README.md Results."))
